# .NET backend

EnterpriseStarter is a PostgreSQL modular monolith with a thin executable host and compile-time modules.

## Entry point

`apps/api/Program.cs` is thin: ServiceDefaults → `AddEnterprisePlatform` → optional migrate/seed → pipeline.
Compose migrator sets `Database:ExitAfterMigrate=true` and returns without listening.

## Structure

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `apps/api` | Composition root, configuration, Docker image |
| `apps/platform` | Identity, global RBAC, controllers, data, audit, migrations |
| `apps/module-abstractions` | `IEnterpriseModule` and production registry |

## JSON

Camel case via `AddJsonOptions`.

## Dev docs

`UseEnterprisePlatform` maps OpenAPI + Scalar in Development only.

## Health

- `/health` — Aspire defaults (dev)
- `/health/ready` — DB check (Compose API healthcheck)

## Reverse proxy / Docker

When TLS terminates at nginx, set `DisableHttpsRedirection=true`. API still uses forwarded headers + HSTS. Cookie secure policy via `Auth:CookieSecurePolicy`.

Product APIs use explicit `/api/v1` routes. Register modules in `ModuleRegistry.Production`; do not scan assemblies or load runtime plugins. Keep browser auth on the application cookie and CSRF protocol.
